# Copy to `.provision.env` (git-ignored, keep it mode 0600) — or let `pnpm provision tokens` write
# it for you (it prompts with hidden input). Read ONLY by `pnpm provision` (apps/web/scripts/
# provision.ts): the account-level tokens that create your Neon project, Cloudflare resources and
# Resend domain. NOT `.dev.vars` — that file is loaded into the Worker by `wrangler dev`, and these
# tokens must never reach a Worker. An exported environment variable of the same name overrides a
# value here (CI exports them; the file is for people). Values are never printed.
# Never paste other environments' credentials into comments: a comment is still a credential on disk.

# --- Provisioning tokens (all four; `--skip-email` makes RESEND_API_KEY optional) -------------
# https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens — Account: Workers Scripts, Workers KV Storage,
# Queues, Workflows, Durable Objects, Hyperdrive, R2 (Edit); Workers AI, Account Analytics (Read).
# Zone: DNS (Edit) on the zone holding your hosts and the sending domain.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# Workers & Pages → Overview, right-hand column (32 hex).
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# https://console.neon.tech/app/settings/api-keys — personal or organisation key.
NEON_API_KEY=
# https://resend.com/api-keys — the FULL-ACCESS account key: it creates the domain and mints the
# per-environment sending key. The app's own sending key is minted by `pnpm provision email verify`
# and set on the Worker with `wrangler secret put`; it is never written here.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# --- Optional Worker secrets copied by `pnpm provision secrets <env>` when set ----------------
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAILS=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
EMBEDDINGS_API_KEY=
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
